ds it up: the bookings, the rental days, the rental charges shown, and how many amounts are still to come with a statement. Your share and every deduction are on your statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Calendar: this month and next</b>, at the bottom, shows the same bookings on a month calendar.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:980/1092"><img src="/guides/img/owner-04-calendar-desktop-be31cbae.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="980" height="1092"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:53.1%;top:15.8%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:12.2%;top:94.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A booking can show as Booked, with its dates and no amount: its amounts show once we approve the statement that covers it, and your statement carries every booking you can see, and every booking paid by the renter. The only bookings left out are an insurance replacement we hide from you and an insurer-billed rental that does not block your car&#39;s calendar: they are not part of your revenue, so they stay off your statements and payouts, and you see only that the car is unavailable for those dates. If one of them later starts counting, you get the new booking email then. Unavailable is time your car is in use by us with no revenue for you (for example an insurance hold). A booking expense or a Revenue Share set for one booking is listed on that booking with the reason, and on your statement.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-rental-history" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Rental history</h2><p class="gd-p">Cars &gt; Bookings also has the <b class="gd-ui">Rental history</b>: every rental on your cars.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each line: the booking number, the car and its plate, the pickup and the return, the days, the status and your earnings from your approved statements. Not on an approved statement yet: it says so.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose one car or all, and oldest or newest first. The totals at the top count every rental in the list.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Renter details, payments and deposits are never shown, and a cancelled booking is listed only when a charge was kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="bookings-and-your-own-use-book-your-own-car" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Book your own car</h2><p class="gd-p">You pay no rental charge, fee or deposit. A renter&#39;s confirmed booking comes first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Cars &gt; Bookings and use <b class="gd-ui">Book my own car</b> on the right (or <b class="gd-ui">Book it for myself</b> on the car&#39;s page).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the Vehicle, then the Pickup and Return date and time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Add a Note (optional) for our team.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Book my car</b>. You sign the same agreement a renter signs.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/bookings</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:450/570"><img s