s done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Under the lines, the counts with one button each (failed payments, agreements to countersign, tolls, listings, insurance, staff commissions, prices typed by hand, sales claims, Turo emails). A count with nothing waiting moves to the bottom, under &quot;more with nothing waiting&quot;.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">While no assistant holds customer service, sales, finance or fleet (the live verification&#39;s test accounts do not count), their tasks come to To do too, and so do their emails, to rent@carmacars.ca.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Beside the list (under it on a phone): today&#39;s pickups (ready or not ready), today&#39;s returns (due or late) and today&#39;s chauffeur bookings, by time.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Overview</b> for the money, fleet and queue figures, the alerts and the team&#39;s sales for the month.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">The dark band at the top counts the day, each count one tap from its page: requests waiting (with how long the oldest has waited, red past the reply target), pickups and returns today, payments to chase, deposits to settle, staff tasks open and alerts. A count that needs you now is red and says so.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/900"><img src="/guides/img/admin-01-today-desktop-ea48309c.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="900"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.9%;top:65%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:61.8%;top:65.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.4%;top:56.1%" aria-hidden="true">5</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:84.4%;top:24.7%" aria-hidden="true">6</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:58.3%;top:37.8%" aria-hidden="true">7</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-the-menu" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The menu</h2><p class="gd-p">Today and Bookings open to show their pages; Cars, People, Marketing, Money and Settings are one link each, which opens the area&#39;s main page with a row of its pages on top. On a phone the whole menu sits behind one Menu button that says where you are.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Menu</th><th scope="col">Pages (the row on top, then a page&#39;s tabs)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Today</td><td>To do, Overview, Staff tasks, Visitors (tabs Live now, Chat, History)</td></tr><tr><td>Bookings</td><td>Trips: Bookings (Now and All bookings; Send an offer and Add a rental are its buttons), Requests and offers (with Chauffeur), Calendar. Customers: Reviews. Problems: Damage and claims (tabs Damage, Incidents, Claims)</td></tr><tr><td>Cars (opens on Vehicles)</td><td>Vehicles (tabs All cars, Fleet tracking, Calendar sync; Add a car, Rates for many cars and Retire or delete are buttons on All cars), Listings (tabs Listings, Similar cars), Maintenance</td></tr><tr><td>Money (opens on Payments, By day)</td><td>Payments (tabs By day, All payments, Refunds, Deposits, Disputes, Reconciliation), Owner money (tabs Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts), Tolls and tickets, Company (tabs Monthly statements, Company model, Expenses, Commissions, Field pay), Insurers (tabs Rates, Invoices)</td></tr><tr><td>People (opens on Owners, Applications)</td><td>Owners (tabs Applications, Owners, Owner forms, Paid and signed; Add a car for an owner is a button), Partners (tabs Rental partners, Referral partners), Renters (tabs Renters, Leads), Team (tabs Staff and roles, Academy, Hiring, Portals and view as), Investors</td></tr><tr><td>Marketing (opens on Marketplace)</td><td>Marketplace, Ads (tabs Ad listings, Posted ads, Social drafts), Channels (tabs Listing channels, Bookings by channel), Owner recruitment (tabs Recruitment, Owner pipeline)</td></tr><tr><td>Settings (opens on Settings)</td><td>Settings (every setting in six sections, with a search box), Logs (tabs Emails, Blocked addresses, Changes, Data access)</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--phone"><div class="gd-phone"><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:390/715"><img src="/guides/img/admin-31-menu-phone-667dc2fd.jpg" alt="On a phone: press Menu (1), then a group (2), then the page (3)." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="390" height="715"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:10.3%;top:28.7%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:42.4%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:76.9%;top:48.3%" aria-hidden="true">3</span></div></div><figcaption>On a phone: press Menu (1), then a group (2), then the page (3).</figcaption></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-tabs-on-a-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Tabs on a page</h2><p class="gd-p">A menu link such as <b class="gd-ui">Money</b> opens a page with a row on top: the area&#39;s name in capitals, then its pages (Payments, Owner money, Tolls and tickets...). The page you are on is black. A page with tabs (such as <b class="gd-ui">Owner money</b>: Invoices, Debits, Statements, Payouts) has a second row under it, the tab you are on outlined in red. On a phone each row slides sideways.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press a tab to change what the page shows. Each tab has its own address, so a link or a bookmark to a tab opens that tab.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An old address (an email or a bookmark from before November 2026, such as Owner invoices, the Audit log or Live chat) opens the page and the tab that now holds it. Each area lists at most five pages; a page that does one thing (Add a car, Send an offer) is a button on the page it belongs to.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Ctrl+K lists every tab and every such button too: type Debits, Field pay or Add a car and press Enter.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-search" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Search</h2><p class="gd-p">The search box sits at the top of the menu, on every page.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Type a booking number (CC-1042), a car code (CC-7F3A, on every car page and fleet card), a plate, a VIN, or a name or email address.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> (or Enter). Results come in groups: bookings, cars, owners, partners and renters. Open one to go to its page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The same box finds pages too: type a few letters (Payouts, Program settings) and the matching pages show above the records. Ctrl+K (Cmd+K on a Mac) or <b class="gd-ui">/</b> puts you in the box from anywhere.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/search?q=CC-10065</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/420"><img src="/guides/img/admin-32-search-desktop-ca548a70.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="420"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:7.4%;top:45.2%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:95%;top:46.9%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-keyboard-shortcuts" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Keyboard shortcuts</h2><p class="gd-p">Press g, then a letter. Press / to jump to the search box, and Ctrl+K to jump to any page.</p><div class="gd-tablewrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Table"><table class="gd-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Keys</th><th scope="col">Opens</th><th scope="col">Keys</th><th scope="col">Opens</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>g t</td><td>To do</td><td>g v</td><td>Cars (Vehicles)</td></tr><tr><td>g r</td><td>Requests</td><td>g o</td><td>People (Owners)</td></tr><tr><td>g b</td><td>Bookings</td><td>g m</td><td>Money (Payments)</td></tr><tr><td>g c</td><td>Calendar</td><td>g k</td><td>Staff tasks</td></tr><tr><td>g s</td><td>Settings</td><td>/</td><td>Search</td></tr><tr><td>Ctrl K</td><td>Search pages and records</td><td>Esc</td><td>Close it</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="gd-h3">Search everything from the header</h3><p class="gd-p">The <b class="gd-ui">Search</b> button at the top of every page (or press <b class="gd-ui">/</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Ctrl K</b>) finds pages, cars, places and guides, and your records: bookings and requests by number, renter name, email, phone or plate, renters, owners and cars. Arrows choose, <b class="gd-ui">Enter</b> opens, <b class="gd-ui">Esc</b> closes. Each person finds only what their role may open.</p></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-one-portal-several-roles-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">One portal, several roles (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">An account with more than one role (Sales and Field work, an owner who is also staff, an Admin who owns a car) no longer chooses between portals after signing in.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Signing in opens the role you used last on this device (the first time: your first role).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Working as</b>, at the top of every page, lists every role of the account: Admin, Customer service, Sales, Fleet, Finance, Field work, Investor, Owner and My rentals, each only if you have it. The role you are in is black. Press another to work in it.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Pages of your other roles</b>, under it, opens the most used pages of the roles you are not in right now, so you can go straight to one.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Nothing about access changed: each page still checks the role, and a page of a role you do not have is still refused. An account with one role sees no switcher.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>An Admin account has no renter portal: My rentals is not offered, and <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/account</span> opens Admin. The renter profile and its bookings stay on file under <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Renters</b>.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="getting-around-admin-unfinished-rentals-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Unfinished rentals (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">Rentals started with <b class="gd-ui">Add a rental</b> and not finished are listed in one place for you: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b> (To do) and <b class="gd-ui">Bookings</b>. Each line says who saved it last and when, what is still missing, whether the car is held, and <b class="gd-ui">Finish it</b>. More than five: the older ones are under <b class="gd-ui">Show older</b>. Sales see the same list on their Today and Bookings. The Add a rental and Send an offer forms no longer carry everyone&#39;s list: they show one line with your own unfinished ones.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'calendars', 'chapter', 'requests-offers-and-bookings', 'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance (blue stripes), not blocking, placeholder, block, Turo and dates taken.
4. Each row is a car, with its photo, code and plate. Bars are bookings and blocks in the Now view''s colours (out red, booked black); the red line is now and today is the black day at the top. Bookings that hold the car run along the top; requests, offers, bookings that do not block and placeholders run underneath. Bars for the same days sit one under the other, never on top of each other.
5. A bar with a red ring and **!** has its dates taken: a request or offer over a booked car or a block. Open it to see what it clashes with, then offer another car or other dates. A placeholder (dashed grey) never clashes with anything.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.6 20.0, 2 47.9 20.0, 3 38.9 31.4, 4 62.5 44.7")

6. Tap a bar for its details in a side panel (on a phone it opens from the bottom). On a phone the calendar opens on **Agenda**: the bookings and blocks by day, each with the car''s photo, the times and its status.

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip a cleaning block holds the car for its turnaround time. It follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Remove it from the side panel if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

![](/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar; pins: 1 46.5 35.5, 2 50.1 46.2")
', 'Calendars', 'The master calendar, moving bookings, blocks, cleaning time and a car''s calendar.',
  'The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.

## Which cars are free (release 44)

At the top of **Calendar**: choose the **Pickup** and the **Return** the customer wants and you see every car at once.

1. Each car says **Available** (green edge) or **Not available** (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the **Next free** start for the same length of rental.
2. An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.
3. Narrow it with **Class**, **Seats at least** and **Price a day up to**, or tick **Available only**.
4. Press **Offer these dates** on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.
5. No customer''s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.

## Find a car in a long fleet (release 48)

With many cars the calendar is one long list. The second row of the toolbar cuts it down.

1. **Search** takes a car, a plate, a fleet number, a booking number or a surname.
2. Filter by **Car status**, **Class**, **Owned by** and **Availability** (Available now, Free today, Free every day shown, Out or booked now, Blocked, in shop or on hold, Not bookable). A filter that is on shows with a black edge; **Clear** takes them all off. Not blocking, Insurer and who supplies the car are under **More filters**.
3. **Group by** Class, Owner, Car status or Availability puts the cars under headings. Each heading says how many cars it has and how many are free today. Press a heading to fold its cars away; **Fold every group** folds them all. Your grouping and the folded groups are remembered in this browser.
4. The count on the right says how many cars show out of all of them, and how many are free today.
5. The list stays fast with a hundred cars or more: only the cars near the screen are drawn as you scroll.

## The master calendar

1. Move through time with the arrows and **Today**, or pick a date.
2. Choose the range: **Today**, **Week**, **2 weeks** or **Month**. **Agenda** shows a list instead.
3. The legend: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance (blue stripes), not blocking, placeholder, block, Turo, dates taken, and the two jobs at the end of a trip: the return check-out and the post-trip cleaning.
4. Each row is a car, with its photo, code and plate. Bars are bookings and blocks in the Now view''s colours (out red, booked black); the red line is now and today is the black day at the top. Bookings that hold the car run along the top; requests, offers, bookings that do not block and placeholders run underneath. Bars for the same days sit one under the other, never on top of each other.
5. A bar with a red ring and **!** has its dates taken: a request or offer over a booked car or a block. Open it to see what it clashes with, then offer another car or other dates. A placeholder (dashed grey) never clashes with anything.

![](/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 1000; address: carmacars.ca/admin/calendar; pins: 1 23.6 20.0, 2 47.9 20.0, 3 38.9 31.4, 4 62.5 44.7")

6. Tap a bar for its details in a side panel (on a phone it opens from the bottom). A booking says **Pickup (check-in)** and **Return (check-out)**: once the car is back, the return shows the time it actually came back, with the time it was due beside it. On a phone the calendar opens on **Agenda**: the bookings, blocks and jobs by day, each with the car''s photo, the times and its status.

## The two jobs at the end of a trip (release 48)

A return is a check-out, never a check-in. Under the bars, each trip that ends in the days shown has two small named chips, each its own job:

1. **Check-out** with its time: when the car is due back, or, once it is back, when it actually came back (the chip then has a tick). It carries who is assigned when a field job exists.
2. **Cleaning**: the post-trip cleaning, with its window (the car''s turnaround time). It has a tick once the clean check after the return is recorded.
3. Tap a chip for its details and its booking. Chips at the same time sit one above the other.

## Move a booking, add or remove a block

1. To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press **Confirm the move**.
2. To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press **Create the block**. **New block** at the top does the same.
3. To remove a block, open it and press **Remove the block**.

> Tip: After every confirmed trip the post-trip cleaning holds the car for its turnaround time. It shows as the **Cleaning** chip, follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Open the chip and press **Remove the block** if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.

## A car''s own calendar

**Cars** > **Vehicles**, then the car, then its Calendar tab.

1. The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.
2. Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press **Change** to give this car its own time.

![](/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar; pins: 1 46.5 35.5, 2 50.1 46.2")
',
  '<p class="gd-p">The master calendar shows every car, booking, request and block. Each car also has its own calendar and turnaround time.</p><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-which-cars-are-free-release-44" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Which cars are free (release 44)</h2><p class="gd-p">At the top of <b class="gd-ui">Calendar</b>: choose the <b class="gd-ui">Pickup</b> and the <b class="gd-ui">Return</b> the customer wants and you see every car at once.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Each car says <b class="gd-ui">Available</b> (green edge) or <b class="gd-ui">Not available</b> (red edge), available cars first. A car that is not available says why: Booked, On rent, Booked, payment due, Placeholder (held), Maintenance, Cleaning, Blocked, Out of service or Leaving the fleet, with the booking number and the dates. It also says the <b class="gd-ui">Next free</b> start for the same length of rental.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">An offer or a request out on a car does not hold it: it shows as a note, and the car stays Available until the booking is paid.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Narrow it with <b class="gd-ui">Class</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Seats at least</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Price a day up to</b>, or tick <b class="gd-ui">Available only</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Offer these dates</b> on an available car. Send an offer opens with the car and the dates filled in; add the customer and send.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">No customer&#39;s name or number is shown here. The answer is the same check the booking makes, so a car shown Available can be booked for those dates.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-find-a-car-in-a-long-fleet-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Find a car in a long fleet (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">With many cars the calendar is one long list. The second row of the toolbar cuts it down.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Search</b> takes a car, a plate, a fleet number, a booking number or a surname.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Filter by <b class="gd-ui">Car status</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Class</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Owned by</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Availability</b> (Available now, Free today, Free every day shown, Out or booked now, Blocked, in shop or on hold, Not bookable). A filter that is on shows with a black edge; <b class="gd-ui">Clear</b> takes them all off. Not blocking, Insurer and who supplies the car are under <b class="gd-ui">More filters</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Group by</b> Class, Owner, Car status or Availability puts the cars under headings. Each heading says how many cars it has and how many are free today. Press a heading to fold its cars away; <b class="gd-ui">Fold every group</b> folds them all. Your grouping and the folded groups are remembered in this browser.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">The count on the right says how many cars show out of all of them, and how many are free today.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">The list stays fast with a hundred cars or more: only the cars near the screen are drawn as you scroll.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-the-master-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The master calendar</h2><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Move through time with the arrows and <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, or pick a date.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Choose the range: <b class="gd-ui">Today</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Week</b>, <b class="gd-ui">2 weeks</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Month</b>. <b class="gd-ui">Agenda</b> shows a list instead.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">The legend: on rent, confirmed, request, offer or hold, maintenance (blue stripes), not blocking, placeholder, block, Turo, dates taken, and the two jobs at the end of a trip: the return check-out and the post-trip cleaning.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Each row is a car, with its photo, code and plate. Bars are bookings and blocks in the Now view&#39;s colours (out red, booked black); the red line is now and today is the black day at the top. Bookings that hold the car run along the top; requests, offers, bookings that do not block and placeholders run underneath. Bars for the same days sit one under the other, never on top of each other.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">A bar with a red ring and <b class="gd-ui">!</b> has its dates taken: a request or offer over a booked car or a block. Open it to see what it clashes with, then offer another car or other dates. A placeholder (dashed grey) never clashes with anything.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/1000"><img src="/guides/img/admin-06-calendar-desktop-fed75400.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="1000"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:23.6%;top:20%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:47.9%;top:20%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:38.9%;top:31.4%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:62.5%;top:44.7%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol" start="6"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Tap a bar for its details in a side panel (on a phone it opens from the bottom). A booking says <b class="gd-ui">Pickup (check-in)</b> and <b class="gd-ui">Return (check-out)</b>: once the car is back, the return shows the time it actually came back, with the time it was due beside it. On a phone the calendar opens on <b class="gd-ui">Agenda</b>: the bookings, blocks and jobs by day, each with the car&#39;s photo, the times and its status.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-the-two-jobs-at-the-end-of-a-trip-release-48" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The two jobs at the end of a trip (release 48)</h2><p class="gd-p">A return is a check-out, never a check-in. Under the bars, each trip that ends in the days shown has two small named chips, each its own job:</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Check-out</b> with its time: when the car is due back, or, once it is back, when it actually came back (the chip then has a tick). It carries who is assigned when a field job exists.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Cleaning</b>: the post-trip cleaning, with its window (the car&#39;s turnaround time). It has a tick once the clean check after the return is recorded.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Tap a chip for its details and its booking. Chips at the same time sit one above the other.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-move-a-booking-add-or-remove-a-block" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Move a booking, add or remove a block</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">To move a booking, drag its bar to the new car or time, then press <b class="gd-ui">Confirm the move</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">To block a car, double-click its row where the block starts, then press <b class="gd-ui">Create the block</b>. <b class="gd-ui">New block</b> at the top does the same.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">To remove a block, open it and press <b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b>.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Tip</span><div>After every confirmed trip the post-trip cleaning holds the car for its turnaround time. It shows as the <b class="gd-ui">Cleaning</b> chip, follows changes and extensions and goes away with a cancellation. Open the chip and press <b class="gd-ui">Remove the block</b> if the car is ready sooner; that time is then free.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="calendars-a-car-s-own-calendar" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">A car&#39;s own calendar</h2><p class="gd-p"><b class="gd-ui">Cars</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Vehicles</b>, then the car, then its Calendar tab.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">The Calendar tab shows only this car, with its bookings and blocks.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Turnaround between trips on this car shows the time used. Press <b class="gd-ui">Change</b> to give this car its own time.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/admin/vehicles/b37ead6c-6196-4cd6-92ff-a14a55a8d5f2?tab=calendar</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/560"><img src="/guides/img/admin-07-vehicle-calendar-desktop-98586ca8.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="560"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:46.5%;top:35.5%" aria-hidden="true">1</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:50.1%;top:46.2%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'owners-and-onboarding', 'chapter', 'chauffeur-service', 'Owners apply on the site with List your car. Every application waits for you in one place, Applications: approve it, ask the owner for something, or decline it. Approved owners sign and pay in their portal.

## Applications

**People** > **Applications**. Every owner application, newest first.

1. The chips filter by status: New, Waiting on owner, Approved, Declined, or All. New applications also show on To do.
2. Each row shows the application number, the owner, the car, how many of the four checks are done, and when they applied.
3. Open an application to decide.

![](/guides/img/admin-33-applications-desktop-152f9e34.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 640; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications; pins: 1 36.8 39.7, 2 48.6 53.1, 3 19.8 53.1")

## Decide on an application

One page holds everything: the owner, the car, the uploads, the four checks and the notes.

1. Check the driver''s licence, the ownership, the insurance and the lender or lessor. Mark each one Checked, fine, Problem or Not needed.
2. Press **Approve**. The step "Terms and first invoice" opens for each car, filled in with the owner''s negotiated terms (or the standard grid): Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and the first and last month amount (2 x the Insurance Fee unless you type an exact amount). Change any of them to the cent; with several cars, **Use these terms for every car** copies the first car''s numbers to the others.
3. Choose the invoices: First and last month, Registration fee (any exact amount), Tracker install (only once trackers are available) and Another invoice. For each one choose Send now, Save as draft or Already paid. Already paid asks how (e-Transfer, cash, cheque, bank transfer or other), the date and the reference: it is recorded like Record payment and the owner gets no email (no invoice, no receipt) unless you tick the receipt.
4. Press **Approve** at the bottom of the step. Nothing is set or sent before that. The owner becomes active, the documents open for one signature in their portal, only the invoices you chose are made, and the owner gets one email.
5. Missing something? Press **Ask for something**, tick what you need (for example the ownership permit or the insurance slip), add a message if you like, and press **Send to the owner**. The owner gets an email and a task in their portal; the application shows Waiting on owner until they answer.
6. Not a fit? Press **Decline**, write the Reason the owner reads, and press **Decline the application**. The owner is emailed for each car.

![](/guides/img/admin-34-application-desktop-98b64f92.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 812; address: carmacars.ca/admin/applications/c324ef8d-ad00-4bcc-bf04-ca68628a26b4; pins: 1 72.9 67.1, 2 73.9 42.9, 3 84.7 42.9, 4 72.9 49.6")

The application has an Invoices tab: every invoice of its cars, drafts and voids included. An application staff entered for the owner says "Entered by staff" and who; approving it sends the owner the set-up email (review the details and sign) instead of the approval email.

> Tip: Notes on the page are for staff only: **Add note** keeps a line on the record. When the owner answers a request, their answer is in the notes and the application is New again.

## Add a car for an owner

**People** > **Owners**, the **Add a car** tab, or **Add another car** on an owner''s page. The owner never has to fill in the application.

1. The owner: find them by name, email or phone, or choose New owner and enter the name, email, phone and address.
2. The car: press **Take a photo** (or **Choose a photo**) under Fill this from the ownership permit, and the plate, VIN, colour, permit number and plate sticker expiry fill in, with the year, make, model code and body read for you to check. Each detail shows Checked, Check this (for example a VIN that fails its check digit, a plate not in the usual format, or a sticker already expired) or Type it; the photo is attached as the ownership permit. Or type the VIN. The car is looked up at once and shown in one line (Edit if something is wrong); no VIN at hand, add it by its plate with the year, make and model from the lists. Tap the colour, check the class, then the odometer, insurer and whether it is owned, financed or leased. Photos are optional: the listing shows sample photos until real ones are added. Upload the ownership permit, the insurance slip and the lender''s information if you have them.
3. Terms and first invoice: the same fields as Approve. For another car of the same owner they start from that owner''s terms, or their other car''s; change them for this car.
4. Who sourced the owner: Entered for CarmaCars, or I sourced this owner (only then are you recorded as the one who brought the owner). The owner signs in the owner portal after one email (no paper signature).
5. Press **Add the car and set it up**. The owner gets one email: review the details, correct anything, and sign. An owner with no sign-in gets the link to choose a password in that same email.

Customer service and fleet assistants add cars the same way from their portal; theirs wait in Applications for you, with the terms and invoices they proposed already filled in. On an approved application staff entered, **Send the set-up email again** sends the owner the email with a fresh link.

## Owners

**People** > **Owners**. Every owner, with their cars and where onboarding stands.

1. Each owner shows their application, how many cars, and where onboarding stands.
2. **View as (owner portal)** shows their portal. **Send password link** helps them sign in.
3. Invite an owner on file: fill in Name and Email under Invite an owner, then press **Send invitation**.

![](/guides/img/admin-12-owners-desktop-3a54d505.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners; pins: 1 41.0 42.9, 2 37.4 49.3, 3 77.4 82.5")

The owner signs everything at once in their portal (Check and sign: the agreements, schedules and Forms A and B; the official registry forms are printed and signed in ink). The confirmations to tick, then one signature: CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment, under the signing officer''s standing authorization. A car with a second owner on the ownership waits for that owner too: they get their own link by email and sign the same documents.

## Mark a car insured (Insurer confirmed)

A program owner''s car is handed over to a renter only once the insurer confirms in writing that it is on the fleet policy. Requests, offers and payment never wait for it.

1. Each car waiting for the insurer is a line on To do: "Insurer has not confirmed : mark it insured". It says Now when a booking picks the car up soon.
2. When the insurer''s email arrives, press **Mark insured**. The date is today; change it to the date of the insurer''s email if it was earlier. Add its subject as the Reference if you like, and press **Insurer confirmed**.
3. One email for several cars? Press **Mark several insured** on the line " cars wait for the insurer". Every waiting car is ticked: untick any car the insurer did not name, check the date, and confirm them all at once.
4. The same button is on the car: Overview (**Insurer confirmed**) and the Listing tab''s checklist, item "Not on the fleet insurance policy yet".

The car is then on the fleet policy from that date: it can be handed over, its Enrollment Date is that date, its fee terms start, and the owner gets the email "Written confirmation: your car is on the fleet policy". Its paperwork (agreements, registry visit, tracker) stays on its checklist until done. A car already listed and Available stays Available.

## Owners who paid another way, and the terms you agreed

Two lines on To do keep an owner''s money right without opening their page.

1. "Record the first and last month paid by ": their first and last month invoice was voided and nothing paid is recorded. Press **Record what they paid**, type the amount for each car (tax included), or one total for several cars, how and when it was paid and the reference. A draft first and last month invoice is kept or voided, your choice. Each car''s invoice is then marked paid and the two prepaid months count; the owner gets no email unless you tick **Email the owner a receipt**. Never for a shareholder.
2. "Enter the terms agreed with ": their cars still use the standard grid. Press **Enter the terms**: the Management fee (Revenue Share), the Insurance Fee, the Tracker Fee, the Install Fee and the first and last month are filled in from the grid. Type what you agreed for the owner, and open a car to give it its own. A car whose schedule is signed gets an updated schedule for the owner to sign.
3. Nothing to change? Press **Not needed** or **These are correct**: the line does not come back.

## A shareholder''s own car

On the owner''s page, each car has **Shareholder’s own car**.

1. A shareholder''s own car is split 90/10 (the share in Program settings) and pays no Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, first and last month or tracker install.
2. Press **Shareholder’s own car**, say why (it is kept in the audit log) and confirm. Press it again to undo. Bookings already made keep their split.
3. A first and last month or a tracker install invoice is refused for such a car, from any screen.

## Cancellation refunds

**Settings** > **Program**: the refund for each cancellation tier.

| When the renter cancels | Refund (default) |
| --- | --- |
| Within 24 hours of booking, 48 hours or more before the start | 95% |
| 48 hours or more before the start | 75% |
| 24 to 48 hours before the start | 50% |
| Under 24 hours, or after the start | 0% |

## An owner''s page

Open an owner from Owners. Three tabs: Overview, Terms and Invoices. **Add another car** and **New invoice** sit under the name.

1. The **Onboarding checklist**, at the top: per car still onboarding, each step done, to do (with who it waits on: the owner, us, an Admin or the registry), blocked (with why) or not needed, and one button for the next thing to do. The owner and customer service see the same checklist.
2. Cars and terms: each car''s Insurance Fee, Tracker Fee, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and mode, with **Edit** and History (see An owner''s terms, car by car).
3. **Onboarding photos**: the ownership permit, insurance slip and lender''s permission of each car. **Replace**, **Remove** (with a reason), **Approve** or **Not accepted** (the owner reads why). A replaced photo that was approved is checked again. Every change is in the audit log.
4. **Government forms**: the ServiceOntario forms each car needs, made by themselves when the terms are approved and again when a value changes, each with its status, what it misses, when it was made and its download. **Make again** makes a car''s forms anew now (a form signed in ink is kept); the values changed by hand stay, unless you tick **Discard the values changed by hand**. Open a form and press **Change a value** to correct one box of the official form before it is signed: choose the box, type the value and the reason. The form is made again as a new version; the earlier versions stay under **Versions**, each with its download, and every change is in the audit log. **Back to the records** puts a box''s value from the records again. The owner always sees the current version only. Fleet can do the same. The owner signs each form on screen during onboarding. Beside the form, **Owner''s signature** shows the drawn signature (or typed name), who signed, when, from which IP address and device, and the version signed; the signature is never on the official form, and **Download the print-ready form** has no signature. If you change a value after the owner signed, the form shows **Changed since signed** with the boxes that changed, the owner gets one To do (the government forms step opens again) and one reminder email, and the earlier signature stays under **Every signature**. The step is done when every form is signed.
5. **Add cars from a list of VINs**: paste or upload the VINs, **Preview**, then **Add**; a typo, a duplicate or a car already with us is reported, not added.
6. Upfront invoices: issue the first and last month amount agreed on each car''s terms, for each car whose terms are set.
7. Owner: address, sign-in and agreements; statements and payouts for this owner.
8. Further down: **View as (owner portal)**, **Send password link** and **Send a sign-in link to the owner portal**.

A car''s page has the same Government forms box (Owner & documents).

![](/guides/img/admin-13-owner-desktop-819a9f8b.jpg "desktop; size: 410 1030; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owners/50a834dc-270a-4c26-b79e-6396fa7bf2e1; pins: 1 24.6 4.4, 2 16.1 32.9, 3 31.5 73.2, 4 21.2 98.1")

## An owner''s terms, car by car

The table Cars and terms, at the top of an owner''s page and its Terms tab: each car''s Insurance Fee and Tracker Fee a month, management fee (Revenue Share), Install Fee and Management Mode, and since when they apply.

1. Press **Edit** on a car''s row. The row becomes fields: type the exact amounts (to the cent; the management fee in %). Before the Vehicle Schedule is signed you can also change the Install Fee, the Management Mode and the Onboarding Method.
2. Press **Review**. It lists each value before and after, and what happens to each one. Nothing is saved yet.
3. Not signed yet (or not approved yet): **Save** applies the numbers at once. An unsigned Vehicle Schedule is made again with them, so the owner signs these numbers; a car not approved yet keeps them for the Approve step.
4. Signed: a lower amount is in force from today, or the date you choose under Lower amounts from. No notice period is needed because it only lowers what the owner pays. A lower management fee does this while Settings > Program, Lower management % without owner signature, is on (the default); off, the owner signs an updated Vehicle Schedule first.
5. Signed: a higher Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee needs 30 days'' written notice (Enrollment Agreement 4.8). Choose the date under Higher amounts from (30 days ahead at the earliest) and write the Reason: the owner reads it.
6. Signed: a higher management fee (Revenue Share) needs the same notice and the owner''s signature. The owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign; it applies from the date once signed, or from the day they sign if that is later. Higher fees in the same change apply from the date by the notice either way.
7. Press **Confirm**. The owner is emailed the written notice, which is also a PDF in their portal and in the car''s History.

History, under each car, lists every period of terms (from, to, the amounts, and why: the Vehicle Schedule, a written notice, lowered) and every change with its notice. A change that has not started yet has Cancel (give the reason): the terms before it run on. An updated schedule waiting for the owner has Withdraw it; the owner signs it in the owner portal (never on paper). One change at a time: cancel or finish the one waiting before making the next.

The same editor is on the car''s page (Records tab, Owner terms). The owner''s default terms (for cars whose terms are set later) and the first and last month invoice stay on the Terms tab.

> Good to know: Invoices follow the dates: a month whose Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee changes part way is billed per day at each rate. The Revenue Share of a rental is the one in force on the day it is booked.

## Pay an owner a flat monthly amount

Some owners want the same amount every month for a car instead of a revenue share and fees. An Admin only, car by car.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Pay** on the car''s row.
2. Choose **Flat monthly payment**, type the **Amount a month** (for example 900.00), the date under **From** and, if it ends, the **Last day**. Write the Reason (kept in the history).
3. Press **Review**: it says what happens and lists any monthly invoice already issued for those days. Then press **Confirm**.
4. From that date the owner''s statement pays the amount every month (a part month by the day), with no revenue share and no Insurance Fee or Tracker Fee. Rentals ending on those days stay with CarmaCars, in the company figures.
5. Back to revenue share: press **Pay**, choose Revenue share and the date. The flat period ends the day before; every period stays in the list.

> Good to know: A month already on an approved owner statement never changes: a new date starts after it. A monthly invoice already issued for flat days stays: void or credit it. A booking expense on a flat car is CarmaCars'' own unless you press **Charge to the owner** beside it on the booking (an Admin only): it is then an owner cost on their statement. Owner costs recorded on the owner''s account (tickets, tolls, damage of their own use) are charged as before.

## Change a signed car''s Management Mode

Managed, Self-Managed or Turo-Only, from a date, for a car whose Vehicle Schedule is signed. An Admin only.

1. Open the owner''s Cars and terms table (or the car''s page) and press **Change mode** on the car''s row.
2. Choose the **New Management Mode** and its Onboarding Method (the options that fit how the car is held), the date under **From**, and write the Reason: the owner reads it. Tick **The owner asked for this** only when it is their own request.
3. Press **Review**: it lists each value before and after (a Self-Managed car has no management fee; a Turo-Only car has no Fees and leaves the fleet insurance policy) and says whether the owner has to sign. Nothing is saved yet.
4. The owner asked and no amount goes up: no signature and no notice period. From today (or the date you chose) the car has the new mode, an updated Vehicle Schedule is issued with CarmaCars'' signature and the owner is emailed the notice.
5. Anything else (CarmaCars'' own decision, or a higher fee): the owner is emailed the notice and an updated Vehicle Schedule to sign, the date is at least 30 days away and the car stays as it is until it is signed. The owner signs it in the owner portal; in History, **Withdraw it** if needed.
6. A change dated ahead applies by itself on its date: the schedule is issued and the car moves. **Cancel** in History (give the reason) stops it and emails the owner that their terms stay as they are. The same email goes when a notice of a higher fee is cancelled.

> Good to know: A shareholder-owned car has fixed terms. A car whose schedule is not signed yet changes its mode in the terms editor, where it applies at once.

## Paid and signed

**People** > **Owners**, the **Paid and signed** tab. What each owner still has to pay or sign, and how each item was done.

1. Each owner shows how many items are open and how many are done. Owners with nothing left are hidden; press Show every owner to see them.
2. Open **Checklist and quick actions**. Each line says Signed in the portal, Signed on paper (before November 2026), Paid by e-Transfer, Not signed, and so on.
3. Paid by e-Transfer, cheque, cash or bank transfer? Press **Record payment**. Choose Paid by, the Date received and the Reference (the cheque number for a cheque). Leave Amount empty for the full balance, or type less for a partial payment. Add a photo of the cheque or a screenshot if you have one.
4. Every agreement is signed in the owner portal: a signature on paper is not recorded. Only an official ServiceOntario form signed in ink is: press **Record an official form signed in ink**, choose the form, check Signed by and Date signed, and upload the scan.
5. The same checklist sits at the top of each owner''s page.
6. You rarely need to come here: an upfront or overdue owner invoice is a line on To do with **Record payment**, and an owner whose documents were sent two days ago or more and are not signed is a line with **Waiting to sign** (open the owner to send the link again). Both pop-ups are the same forms, filled in.

A recorded payment marks the invoice paid (or partly paid), stops the automatic debit for that amount, sends the owner a receipt, and shows "Paid by e-Transfer on " in their portal. An official form recorded as signed in ink counts as signed everywhere: the checklist, onboarding and the owner portal. The scan is kept privately with the owner''s documents.

> Watch out: Recorded the wrong thing, or a cheque bounced? Press **Void** beside it and give the reason. The invoice owes that amount again and the owner is told; a voided signature makes the item open again. Only an Admin can void.

## Forms C and D

**People** > **Owner forms**. Forms C and D are signed on screen in the owner portal, with the witnesses on the same screen (one for Form C, two for Form D), and approved at once; Part 2 of Form D is signed for CarmaCars from the stored signatures (the signing officer, and the second signing officer of Program settings as CarmaCars'' witness). This queue holds only photos of paper copies sent before November 2026.

1. Each row shows the owner, the form, the witnesses and when it was uploaded.
2. Press Open to read the photo or scan. Check each marked spot is signed or initialled.
3. Press **Approve**, or **Send back** with What to fix (the owner reads this).

![](/guides/img/admin-22-owner-forms-desktop-c20ad300.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 470; address: carmacars.ca/admin/owner-forms; pins: 1 29.2 52.3, 2 57.6 52.3, 3 76.7 52.3")

## The earnings calculator on List your car

People who think of listing their car see what it could earn, near the top of List your car and, smaller, at the start of the application. They pick the year, make and model (or type the VIN), the days rented a month (5 to 28, 18 at first) and their share (60% to 90%, 70% at first, "set in your agreement"). The page shows the month and the year: the daily rate of cars like theirs on the site (the same make and model, else the class average, else the class''s starting rate in Program settings) times the days, their share of it, less the monthly fees. "Just cheaper insurance" shows the fleet policy''s fee and what they would keep at only 5 days a month.

1. **Settings** > **Program**: **Earnings calculator on List your car: the monthly insurance fee shown** and **the monthly tracker fee shown**, in dollars a month.
2. Leave either one empty and the page says "Insurance and tracker fees: quoted in your agreement" and shows the earnings "before fees". No amount is ever made up.
3. Set both and the page takes them off the month and the year. Each owner''s real fees stay the ones in their agreement.

## Agreements: who still needs to sign

**Owners and partners** > **Owners** > **Agreements**. Every owner with the agreements their deal needs, and where each one stands.

1. Each owner shows their deal (revenue split, flat monthly or fleet lease) and one line per agreement: the Vehicle Enrollment Agreement, the Flat-Rate Vehicle Enrollment Agreement or the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement, the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, an Additional Vehicle Schedule for a car added later, the Partner agreement, and a Referral Override Agreement for each owner they referred.
2. Each line says **Signed**, **Sent, not signed**, **Not sent** or **Missing**. Missing means there is nothing to sign yet: set the terms of a car first, and the agreement is made from them.
3. Press **Send** (or **Send again**). The owner gets one email with the link to read and sign in their portal. An owner with no sign-in yet shows "invite first": press Invite on the Owners list.
4. Owners whose agreements are all signed are hidden; press Show every owner to see them. The same lines are at the top of each owner''s Terms tab.

> Good to know: "Awaiting lawyer OK" marks the Referral Override Agreement until the lawyer approves its text (Program settings). The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is approved. Owners can sign either way.

## A fleet supplier: the fleet lease

For a supplier''s corporation that leases many cars to CarmaCars. Open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**.

1. A supplier who signs up on the website as a fleet supplier (or whom staff add on the fleet supplier route) gets the default lease terms of Program settings and the default Upkeep Table at once: the card shows **Fleet supplier route**. To agree other numbers, press **Change the lease terms**.
2. A supplier on file without the route: press **Enter the lease terms** and type what you agreed: the Regular Rate and the Troubled Rate (the lease a month for each car of that tier), the Claim Profit Share, the Early Write-Off Share, the Write-Off Period in months, the Later Write-Off Share and the Notice Period in days.
3. Check the **Upkeep Table**: for each cost (engine, transmission, shocks, rustproofing, refurbishment, tires, brakes, oil changes, ball joints) the supplier or CarmaCars.
4. Add each car with **Add another car** on the owner''s page. The **Fleet lease** step asks for the tier (Regular or Troubled) and the delivery date: the tier is required and set once. No fee or invoice step: the supplier pays CarmaCars nothing, and no owner invoice or debit is ever made for these cars.
5. A car already on file: press **Put on the lease** beside it, with the delivery date and the tier.
6. The tier never changes. Typed the wrong one? Only an Admin can press **Correct the tier**, with what was entered by mistake. It is corrected from the delivery (or from the day after the last approved statement) and kept in the audit log.
7. The lease is paid in arrears on the 10th with the owner payouts: a car''s first payment is on the first 10th at least one full month after its delivery and covers every month up to then. Part months are paid by the day; the statement line shows the calculation (rate, days, total).
8. A claim on a leased car: settling it pays the supplier its Claim Profit Share of any profit, on its next statement. A write-off pays any lien first, then the supplier''s Early or Later Write-Off Share of the balance by the months in service.
9. An upkeep cost: **Record an upkeep cost**. A cost the Upkeep Table gives the supplier comes off its next lease payment; one CarmaCars pays is not billed.

> Watch out: New lease terms after the supplier signed wait for the supplier to sign the new agreement (it opens for signature at once). The cars keep the signed rates until then.

## Approve a fleet supplier''s cars

A supplier who signed up on the website: his application is in **Applications** like any other, with each car''s VIN, plate and the tier he chose.

1. Open the application. Check the ownership copy of each car (he uploads it in his portal), the tier and who the car is registered to now. Its ServiceOntario forms were filled in when he added it: the lease (SR-LV-006 with his corporation as the registrant, SR-LV-012 with CarmaCars holding the plates) and, for a car not yet in his corporation, the transfer (ON00453 when the corporation has no RIN; 013-0169 and 013-1155 when an officer moves his own car in). A form still missing a value (a RIN, the odometer) shows what is missing, as on the other routes.
2. A tier chosen by mistake: open the owner, **Terms** tab, **Fleet lease**, and press **Correct the tier** beside the car, with what was chosen by mistake. Only an Admin can, and only before approval; it is kept in the audit log.
3. Approve: there are no terms or invoices to set. Check **Delivered on** (the lease starts that day) and press **Approve**. Each car goes on the lease at its tier.
4. He signs in the owner portal only: the Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement and the Title-Holding and Lease Agreement, and Form B on screen, with the full e-signature and its audit trail. Paper signatures cannot be recorded for him. Form D is in his packet and signed on screen with two witnesses; Form C is not asked.

> Good to know: The Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement is final: the lawyer approved it, so it no longer shows "Awaiting lawyer OK". The default lease terms are in **Settings** > **Program settings** (Fleet supplier route); a change there applies to suppliers who sign up later.

> Good to know: Owners > **Add an owner** offers the same route: choose **A corporation**, then **Fleet supplier: leases the cars to CarmaCars**. So does **Add a car for an owner** for a new owner.
